---
# The C half of the tree: this directory and examples/plugin_c_demo are the only translation units
# the repository compiles as C, and two checks of the root config describe C++ rather than a defect
# here. Scoped to the directory rather than switched off globally, because both are worth keeping
# over the C++ that is the rest of the codebase — including the C++ fixtures next to these C ones,
# which give up little for it.
InheritParentConfig: true

# cppcoreguidelines-init-variables wants an initialiser on every declaration, and these files declare
# at the top of the block and assign below — which is how C reads and, more to the point, what makes a
# use before the assignment a diagnosable mistake rather than a silent zero. Seeding a handle with 0
# would hide exactly the bug the check exists to find.
# cppcoreguidelines-avoid-non-const-global-variables fires on the counters a C fixture keeps: a C
# module has no member to put one in, and the plugin's own file scope is the only place left.
Checks: >
  -cppcoreguidelines-init-variables,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-non-const-global-variables
...
